course: dictionary
lesson: 2277
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Creeper is one of these words.
explain: «At the end he hides the mouth with creepers, brushwood, and dead leaves.» Here creepers are plants that grow along the ground or over things. The clue is hides: the plants cover the tunnel so nobody can see it.
explain: Creeper can also mean a person who behaves in a creepy way, such as someone who watches people in secret. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about plants, birds or people? That one question often settles it.
fact: Creeper is a noun. A creeper is a plant that grows along the ground or climbs up walls, fences and trees, such as ivy.
fact: A treecreeper is a small bird that creeps up tree trunks looking for insects.
fact: In informal speech, a creeper is a person who behaves in a creepy way, for example by watching people secretly.
fact: In old-fashioned English, «creepers» (plural) can mean soft shoes or a baby's one-piece suit. In the US, this is the usual word for these.
fact: Some plants, like the ones in science lessons, climb towards the light using tendrils or little roots.
exercise: In «at the end he hides the mouth with creepers, brushwood, and dead leaves», what are the creepers? | Soft shoes | Dead leaves on the ground | *Plants that grow over things | Small birds
exercise: What is a treecreeper? | A tall tree that grows very fast | A soft baby's suit | A plant with sharp thorns | *A small bird that creeps up tree trunks looking for insects
exercise: Ella says her neighbour is a creeper because he watches people secretly. What does she mean? | A small bird | A pair of soft shoes | A plant that grows up a wall | *A person who behaves in a creepy way
test: Which of these is a creeper plant? | A tall oak tree standing alone | A sheep grazing in a field | A rock sitting in a river | *Ivy growing up a garden wall
test: In old-fashioned English, what can «creepers» mean? | *Soft shoes or a baby's one-piece suit | A ghost | A small bird | A plant
exam: Which meaning fits best in «He crept round the house, watching us through the window every day»? | Plants that cover a wall | *A person who behaves in a creepy way | Soft shoes | A small bird that creeps up trees
